From b63780d87504f0cd65c89adad7ddd61fd9e6afd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:51:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 113/113] Silence: the filters, the EQ and the volume stage
 start from their settings when a kit or audio track sounds again

A kit or audio track whose effects gave out exact silence for 4096 samples skips them: the early return before the
setup (v17), or the check after rendering (v12) where the early return can't be taken. v18's per-sample ramps and
fades kept their state across that silence, and the two ways did different things with it:
- the early return restarted the volume ramps, the check after rendering didn't: a volume changed while silent
  ramped from the old one over at least 5 ms of the next sound there (tests/silent against a v18 reference without
  the early return: up to -21 dBFS from bar 5 on);
- in both, the filters' coefficients moved from the last rendered block, from before the silence; a crossfade
  started while silent stayed frozen (holding one of the 24 slots, and keeping the early return from being taken)
  and ran over the first 7 ms of the next sound; a filter switched on while silent faded in from the dry signal
  there; the EQ's gain and corner moved from before the silence.
Now both call the same: the filter params stop gliding, FilterSet::restartAfterSilence() (no ramp from the last
rendered configuration or gain compensation, a crossfade ends and frees its slot, no switch-on fade-in), and
ModControllableAudio::restartAfterSilence() (the volume ramps and the EQ bands take their gains and corners at once).
A sound that stops rendering restarts its EQ too.

tests/silent against the same source with the early return disabled: the same output, sample for sample (705,654
samples), the same 116 arpeggiator notes; 26,118 early returns (25,769 before: LREV's frozen crossfade no longer
keeps it from them). Against v18: from bar 4.5 on, where tracks sound again after changes while silent (-40 dBFS in
the first 2.5 ms at 4.5, -34 dBFS at 5 through the delay's repeats).

